{"base_rate":0.12957317073170732,"brier":0.0551984756097561,"bss":0.5105822355001546,"bss_hi":0.5982469343213753,"bss_lo":0.4325613687972926,"chart":{"base":[230.0,48.7],"fp":[215.7,403.9],"lead":"62,247.6 272,223 482,181 692,118.2","note":{"base":"skill 0.51 — higher than 92% of cities","fp":"low end +2pp, high end -8pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.1 °C — better than 46% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 1%; promised 44% → rained 53%"},"rel":"62,461.5 95.4,436.8 338,237.3"},"country":"TM","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.027987804878048785,"ess":420.5155190634086,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Ashgabat</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Ashgabat rain forecast is strongly skilful, though 2 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (65%), believe about\n<b>78%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>1%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 656 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-03-26. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 2.2 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.51, ranked 17 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(6&ndash;43) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>1%</b></td><td class='num'>387</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>3%</td><td class='num'><b>4%</b></td><td class='num'>53</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>7%</td><td class='num'><b>9%</b></td><td class='num'>80</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>20%</td><td class='num'><b>25%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>65%</td><td class='num'><b>78%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">2 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Ashgabat</b> <span class=\"muted\">Turkmenistan</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Strongly skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">2 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.51</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>6&ndash;43\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>656 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Ashgabat &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Ashgabat\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" 