87 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"378.2377260981912\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 3%&amp;#10;It rained 4% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 53 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"68.62\" cy=\"368.2641509433962\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 7%&amp;#10;It rained 9% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 80 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"82.1605\" cy=\"350.15\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 20%&amp;#10;It rained 25% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 64 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"129.2425\" cy=\"291.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 65%&amp;#10;It rained 78% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"287.65749999999997\" cy=\"98.88888888888886\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(13%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Ashgabat the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.57) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.20).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>171</td><td class='num'>2%</td><td class='num'>0.197</td><td class='num'>1.5%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>147</td><td class='num'>22%</td><td class='num'>0.360</td><td class='num'>7.1%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>167</td><td class='num'>22%</td><td class='num'>0.560</td><td class='num'>5.6%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>171</td><td class='num'>7%</td><td class='num'>0.570</td><td class='num'>0.6%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":37.95,"lon":58.38333,"n":656,"n_cities":213,"name":"Ashgabat","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":387,"obs":0.0103359173126615,"sig":true},{"hi":0.05,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.030000000000000002,"n":53,"obs":0.03773584905660377,"sig":false},{"hi":0.13,"lo":0.05,"mean":0.06825,"n":80,"obs":0.0875,"sig":false},{"hi":0.35,"lo":0.13,"mean":0.20124999999999998,"n":64,"obs":0.25,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.35,"mean":0.6487499999999999,"n":72,"obs":0.7777777777777778,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":2.2,"provisional":false,"rank":17,"rank_hi":43.02499999999998,"rank_lo":6.0,"reliability":0.0021721469861576384,"resolution":0.056815779589518736,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"ashgabat","station":"","timezone":"Asia/Ashgabat"}